      "settings": {
        "compact": true,
        "eyebrow": "PLATFORM SAFETY",
        "heading": "How to grow without getting your account restricted",
        "body": "<p>Most reseller accounts aren't banned for doing something dishonest. They're restricted because their listing pattern looked automated, or because a payment was taken off-platform. Both are avoidable once you know what the systems are watching for.</p>",
        "primary_label": "Back to Learn Hub",
        "primary_url": "/pages/learn"
      }
    },
    "why": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "settings": {
        "background": "surface",
        "narrow": true,
        "eyebrow": "WHY IT HAPPENS",
        "heading": "The platform isn't judging you. It's pattern-matching.",
        "body": "<p>Vinted in particular is built around the idea of individuals clearing their own wardrobes. When an account starts behaving like a shop - twenty identical items, uploaded in one burst, all brand new with the tags on - automated checks notice. No human decided you were a problem; a pattern did.</p><p>That's good news, because patterns can be changed. Almost everything below is about looking like an enthusiastic individual seller rather than a bulk operation.</p>"
      }
    },
    "triggers": {
      "type": "content-cards",
      "settings": {
        "background": "paper",
        "columns": "2",
        "eyebrow": "WHAT TRIGGERS A FLAG",
        "heading": "The patterns that get accounts restricted",
        "body": "<p>These are the behaviours that most reliably cause trouble, roughly in order of how often they catch people out.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "t1": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "MOST COMMON",
            "heading": "Bulk-uploading identical items in one session",
            "body": "<p>Twenty of the same necklace, posted within an hour, is the single clearest signal that this isn't a personal wardrobe. Spread multiples across days, vary the photo angle and the wording, and list a few genuinely different items in between.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "HIGH RISK",
            "heading": "Taking payment off-platform",
            "body": "<p>Someone asks to pay by bank transfer to save fees. It is the most common way sellers lose both the money and the account. You lose all buyer protection and it breaches the terms of every platform here. Keep every transaction on the platform, every time - no exceptions for someone who seems nice.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "HIGH RISK",
            "heading": "Brand names you can't substantiate",
            "body": "<p>Using a designer or brand name to describe an item that isn't from that brand - even as \"style\" or \"dupe\" - invites both takedowns and legal trouble. Describe what the item genuinely is. If the pack came without brand authorisation, don't borrow a brand's name to sell it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t4": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "MODERATE",
            "heading": "Stock photos instead of your own",
            "body": "<p>Supplier images appear across hundreds of listings, so duplicate-image detection picks them up quickly, and buyers trust them less. Photograph the actual item you're holding. A phone against a plain wall in daylight beats a supplier render every time.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t5": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "MODERATE",
            "heading": "Multiple accounts from one device",
            "body": "<p>Running a second account to get around a limit is usually detected through the device or connection, and typically costs you both accounts. Grow the one account instead.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t6": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "label": "MODERATE",
            "heading": "Slow dispatch and unanswered messages",
            "body": "<p>Not a ban risk on its own, but it quietly suppresses how often you're shown, and it drives the negative feedback that does real damage. Answer within a day; post within your stated window.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "t1",
        "t2",
        "t3",
        "t4",
        "t5",
        "t6"
      ]
    },
